      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "Some context on why I looked at this: a user who moved from Knots to Core reported that Electrum took about one minute to connect to his electrs during the tx spike around block 976230 (50k to 70k small txs in the mempool), and about 2 seconds increasig the tx minimum fee (so less tx on mempool). electrs calls `getrawmempool` in a loop, in the same thread that serves clients, and on Core each of those calls sorts the whole mempool while holding `cs` (76 of 96 ms with 60k txs on x86).",
